+## Turn usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and is handed the usage of every provider call in that turn, summed across tool rounds: for a turn driven through two tool rounds whose provider calls report different token counts, the hook receives the per-field sum of all three calls, so a deployer billing or budgeting from the hook no longer under-counts exactly the turns that ran tools ([validated by: hands the hook the usage of every provider call in the turn, summed across tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L55)).
+- A round that reports no usage contributes nothing to that sum rather than poisoning it — the rounds that did report are still counted — and a turn whose provider calls report no usage at all still hands the hook no usage ([validated by: skips rounds that report no usage, and still reports nothing when no round reports](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L84)).
+- A turn with no tool calls is unchanged: the hook receives exactly what the turn's single provider call reported, so the common path does not move ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
